# SimpleImageConverter — Domain Rules

## Project Identity

- **Project:** SimpleImageConverter
- **Type:** Cross-platform desktop CLI + GUI application (Rust cargo workspace)
- **Purpose:** Batch image and 3D mesh format conversion. Handles 2D formats (PNG, JPEG, BMP, GIF, SVG, TIFF, WebP) and 3D mesh formats (STL, OBJ, PLY, glTF/GLB). Offline, no cloud dependencies.
- **Tone:** Developer/maker tool. Precise, minimal UI. No unnecessary chrome.
- **Active targets:** Windows 11, macOS, Linux (Ubuntu 24.04+) — all active, no phasing.
- **License:** MIT OR Apache-2.0 (dual). All dependencies must be compatible.

## Workspace Architecture

```
SimpleImageConverter/          Workspace root
  common/                      Shared utilities (format detection, path helpers)
  img-core/                    2D image processing library (format decode/encode)
  img-convert/                 2D CLI binary (wraps img-core)
  mesh-core/                   3D mesh processing library
  mesh-convert/                3D CLI binary (wraps mesh-core)
  converter-gui/               egui/eframe GUI (current)
  converter-gui-modern/        Modernised egui GUI (in progress)
  tests/                       Integration tests (shared test data)
  fuzz/                        Fuzzing targets
  scripts/                     Build, packaging, and release scripts
  release/                     Release artefact staging
  AGENT_TASKS/                 Active and historical agent task briefs
```

**Crate responsibilities are strict.** Do not add format-handling logic to CLI
binaries — it belongs in `img-core` or `mesh-core`. Do not add GUI code to library
crates. Keep the dependency graph clean: binaries depend on libs, not vice versa.

## Code Standards

### Rust (all crates)

- **MSRV:** 1.92 (set in `[workspace.package]`). Do not use features introduced
  after 1.92 without bumping MSRV and noting it in the PR.
- **Error handling:** `thiserror` for library error types; `anyhow` for application
  error propagation in binaries and Tauri commands. No `unwrap()` in production
  paths — use `?` with proper context.
- **Documentation:** All public API items must have doc comments with `# Errors`
  sections on fallible functions.
- **Testing:** Unit tests in `#[cfg(test)]` modules; integration tests in `tests/`.
  Add a test for every new format conversion path.
- **Formatting/lint:** `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings`
  must pass before every commit. Zero warnings policy.
- **Benchmarks:** `img-core/benches/` uses Criterion. Add benchmarks for new
  performance-sensitive conversion paths.
- **Fuzzing:** `fuzz/` contains libFuzzer targets. Update fuzz targets when adding
  new format parsers.

### Security (critical — all file input is untrusted)

- **Validate early:** Check file magic bytes / headers before processing. Reject
  malformed input with a clear error, not a panic.
- **Size limits:** Enforce maximum input dimensions and file sizes to prevent
  memory exhaustion (OOM).
- **No `unsafe` without review:** Any new `unsafe` block requires security specialist
  sign-off. Document invariants in a comment above the block.
- **Dependency audit:** Run `cargo audit` before every release. High/critical
  advisories are blocking. Note: `ply-rs` was removed due to CVE-2020-25573 —
  use `ply-rs-bw` instead.
- **Path traversal:** Never construct output paths from user-supplied input without
  sanitisation. Use `std::path::Path::canonicalize` and validate against expected
  output roots.

## Format Support Matrix

| Format | Crate | Read | Write | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| PNG | `image` | ✓ | ✓ | |
| JPEG | `image` | ✓ | ✓ | |
| BMP | `image` | ✓ | ✓ | |
| GIF | `image` | ✓ | ✓ | |
| TIFF | `image` | ✓ | ✓ | |
| WebP | `image` | ✓ | ✓ | |
| SVG | `resvg`/`tiny-skia` | ✓ | ✗ | Rasterise to target format |
| STL | `stl_io` | ✓ | ✓ | Binary and ASCII |
| OBJ | `tobj` | ✓ | ✓ | |
| PLY | `ply-rs-bw` | ✓ | ✓ | Not `ply-rs` — see CVE-2020-25573 |
| glTF/GLB | `gltf` | ✓ | planned | |

Before adding a new format, check `rust-resources.md` for library guidance and verify
the chosen crate supports Windows + macOS + Linux and has a compatible license.

## GUI (egui/eframe)

- `converter-gui` is the current production GUI. `converter-gui-modern` is under
  active development as its replacement — confirm with the user which to target.
- egui renders consistently across platforms via wgpu/OpenGL backends. Platform-specific
  appearance tweaks (HiDPI, dark mode detection) must use egui's `Context` APIs.
- Do not add non-Rust dependencies to the GUI crates. egui is self-contained.
- Test GUI on all three platforms before marking a UI change complete.

## Testing Expectations

- **Unit tests:** In `#[cfg(test)]` modules within each crate. Run: `cargo test --workspace`.
- **Integration tests:** In `tests/` using real image/mesh fixtures from `tests/data/`.
- **Benchmarks:** `cargo bench` in `img-core/`. Do not regress existing benchmarks.
- **Fuzz tests:** `cargo fuzz run <target>` from the `fuzz/` directory. Run locally
  before adding a new format parser.
- Use `#[ignore]` for tests that require platform-specific resources unavailable in CI.
- Document manual test steps in `MANUAL_TESTING_REPORT_SPRINT*.md` for releases.

